  "title": "Any proof that native gadgets cannot clone a bit must be global",
  "subject": "What a proof of the arm inequality for gadgets with loops must contain",
  "conclusion": "Rerouting one terminal's arm is injective for each fixed difference pattern, so the arm inequality holds whenever patterns map injectively, as on trees. For gadgets with loops, explicit two- and three-knot gadgets satisfy the inequality but break every local strengthening (per partner, per image pattern, one-sided path flips, the minor form), so any proof must be global.",
